{"id":56057,"ord":157,"n_segments":180,"prev":56056,"next":56058,"doc":{"id":"68098","title":"68098_Snub Mosley oral history interview","collection":"rutgers","inst":"Rutgers — Institute of Jazz Studies","interviewee":"Snub Mosley","interviewer":"","date":"","year":"","source_url":"https://rucore.libraries.rutgers.edu/rutgers-lib/68098/","url":"https://semlab.io/linked-jazz-transcripts/?t=68098"},"chapter":"Hollywood, Ken Murray and the Penguin years","title":"The One Hundred Club in 1945","category":"venue_city_scene","summary":"A swank 100th Street room where the band broadcasts nationally, with a roster of players.","period":"Nov. 1945","year_from":1945,"year_to":1945,"words":178,"start":[256,3],"end":[258,4],"url":"https://semlab.io/linked-jazz-transcripts/?t=68098#s56057","tags":{"places":[{"name":"Broadway","focus":0,"type":"street","in":"New York"},{"name":"100th Street","focus":0,"type":"street","in":"New York"}],"venues":[{"name":"One Hundred Club","focus":1,"city":"New York"},{"name":"Whitehall Hotel","focus":0,"city":"New York"}],"bands":[{"name":"Snub Mosley's band","focus":1,"leader":"Snub Mosley"}]},"people":[{"name":"Ben Smith","qid":"Q4886485","n":3},{"name":"Bob Carroll","qid":null,"n":2},{"name":"A.G. Godley","qid":"Q115675567","n":2},{"name":"Jimmy Robinson","qid":null,"n":2},{"name":"Smiley Trotman","qid":null,"n":2},{"name":"Lloyd Phillips","qid":"Q41798556","n":1},{"name":"Tommy Benford","qid":"Q431785","n":1}],"story":{"theme":36,"theme_name":"Coming to New York: clubs, jams, and making it","community":73,"community_name":"Making it in New York: arrival, clubs and the scene","core":false},"blocks":[{"p":256,"b":3,"s":"MR. DRIGGS","x":"I know what we missed; Ben Smith. Now let's get him in the picture. Where do we get Ben Smith?"},{"p":256,"b":4,"s":"MR. MOSLEY","x":"When I got back from overseas--"},{"p":256,"b":5,"s":"MR. DRIGGS","x":"The first time; right?"},{"p":256,"b":6,"s":"MR. MOSLEY","x":"'45. I went into the One Hundred Club."},{"p":256,"b":7,"s":"MR. DRIGGS","x":"That's in the Village?"},{"p":256,"b":8,"s":"MR. MOSLEY","x":"No, no, that's 100 and Broadway. When 100th Street was really swanky."},{"p":256,"b":9,"s":"MR. DRIGGS","x":"Broadway and 100th Street?"},{"p":256,"b":10,"s":"MR. MOSLEY","x":"100th Street and Broadway."},{"p":257,"b":0,"s":"MR. DRIGGS","x":"Oh yeah?"},{"p":257,"b":1,"s":"MR. MOSLEY","x":"The One Hundred Club in the Whitehall Hotel. It's a flea place now, but then it was nothing but swanky. That's where we were broadcasting the Associated Broadcasting System network."},{"p":257,"b":2,"s":"MR. DRIGGS","x":"This is 1945?"},{"p":257,"b":3,"s":"MR. MOSLEY","x":"November, '45."},{"p":257,"b":4,"s":"MR. DRIGGS","x":"The band is Bob Carroll; right?"},{"p":257,"b":5,"s":"MR. MOSLEY","x":"Bob Carroll."},{"p":257,"b":6,"s":"MR. DRIGGS","x":"Ben Smith."},{"p":257,"b":7,"s":"MR. MOSLEY","x":"Ben Smith."},{"p":257,"b":8,"s":"MR. DRIGGS","x":"You; Lloyd Phillips?"},{"p":257,"b":9,"s":"MR. MOSLEY","x":"No. Smiley Trotman."},{"p":257,"b":10,"s":"MR. DRIGGS","x":"Smiley Trotman and Jimmy Robinson."},{"p":257,"b":11,"s":"MR. MOSLEY","x":"Jimmy Robinson on bass."},{"p":257,"b":12,"s":"MR. DRIGGS","x":"A.G. Godley."},{"p":257,"b":13,"s":"MR. MOSLEY","x":"A.G. Godley and then I got a little sick of A.G. for a while and got"},{"p":258,"b":0,"s":"MR. MOSLEY","x":"Tommy Benford."},{"p":258,"b":1,"s":"MR. MOSLEY","x":"I've got a picture of that band. Would you want one of them?"},{"p":258,"b":2,"s":"MR. DRIGGS","x":"Yeah."},{"p":258,"b":3,"s":"MR. MOSLEY","x":"I think you got one of those copied already. This is it right here."},{"p":258,"b":4,"s":"MR. MOSLEY","x":"You can keep that."}]}